    {"title":"Bolt the six threaded rods to one side frame","text":"Take one side frame (1) and the 6 rods (2) that have a threaded hole in each end. Place the rods at the front and back of each tier, and fix each one through the post with one bolt A. Tighten the bolts with the Allen key C.","tip":"Use only the rods with the metal threaded insert here. Plain rods cannot be bolted.","warn":null,"need":[["1",1],["2",6],["A",6],["C",1]],"confidence":"high","page":3},
    {"title":"Insert the plain rods","text":"Push the 9 plain rods (3) into the holes in the frame's cross rails, 3 per tier, between the bolted front and back rods.","tip":"Push every rod fully into its hole so all rods line up for the second frame.","warn":null,"need":[["3",9]],"confidence":"high","page":3},
    {"title":"Fit the second side frame and add the pads","text":"Fit the second side frame (1) onto all 15 rod ends. Fix it with 6 bolts A through the posts into the threaded rods, then tighten them with the Allen key. Peel the backing off the 4 pads B and stick one under the bottom of each leg.","tip":"Start all six bolts loosely, check that every plain rod sits in its hole, and only then tighten the bolts.","warn":null,"need":[["1",1],["A",6],["B",4]],"confidence":"medium","page":4}
